# Manifest of the examples shown in the web interface's selector, read by
# src/06-user-interface/web/gen_examples/gen_examples.ml to generate the
# module Examples_tpe (see src/06-user-interface/web/dune).
#
# One example per non-blank, non-comment line, five fields separated by ' | ':
#
#   group | title | grade | path | description
#
# - group: the optgroup label the example is listed under in the selector.
# - title: the option's text, without a prefix already given by the group.
# - grade: the grading monoid the web interface switches to when the example
#   is loaded (a key of Grades.GradeRegistry.grade_modules).
# - path: the example's file, relative to this directory.
# - description: one sentence, shown as the option's tooltip.
#
# Examples are listed in the order they appear in the selector: groups in the
# order given here, and within a group from the simplest example to the most
# advanced.

Basics | Delay | time-lower-bound | basics/delay.tpe | Functions accumulate delays, whether taken directly or hidden in a returned closure.
Basics | Unbox | time-lower-bound | basics/basic_unbox.tpe | Unboxing before the box's grade has accumulated is rejected.
Basics | Folding over boxes | time-lower-bound | basics/fold_over_boxes.tpe | A fold builds a chain of boxed accumulators, each claimed once the grade it demands has accumulated.
Basics | Algebraic operations | time-lower-bound | basics/operations.tpe | Operation calls advance the accumulated grade by their declared cost.
Basics | Top-level structures | time-lower-bound | basics/toplevel.tpe | A polymorphic sum type and a generalised top-level function, folded over a list.
Basics | Natural numbers as an inductive type | time-lower-bound | basics/nat.tpe | Unary natural numbers with addition and multiplication, defined by structural recursion.
Basics | Recursive functions on integers | time-lower-bound | basics/recursion.tpe | Factorial, Fibonacci and Euclid's algorithm, by ordinary recursion.
Basics | Eternal types | time-upper-bound | basics/eternal_types.tpe | Values of eternal types stay usable however much grade accumulates; functions and non-eternal types do not.

Effect handlers | Lower bounds | time-lower-bound | handlers/handlers_lower_bound.tpe | An operation case may resume its continuation once it has waited for at least the operation's grade.
Effect handlers | Upper bounds | time-upper-bound | handlers/handlers_upper_bound.tpe | An operation case may resume its continuation at any point up to the operation's grade, or not at all.
Effect handlers | Nested | time-lower-bound | handlers/handlers_nested.tpe | Nested handlers each resume their own continuation, quantifying over one rigid effect per level of nesting.
Effect handlers | Nested (rejected) | time-lower-bound | handlers/handlers_nested_reject.tpe | The nested-handlers example with one inner continuation left unresumed, correctly rejected.

Time grades | Upper bounds | time-upper-bound | time/time_upper.tpe | A box may be unboxed at any point up to its upper-bound grade.
Time grades | Intervals | time-interval | time/time_intervals.tpe | A box grade pairs a lower and an upper time bound, unboxable only within that interval.

Trace grades | Lower bounds | traces-lower-bound | traces/traces_lower.tpe | A 3D-printing pipeline whose operations must be covered by the runs a box demands, waiting banking towards them.
Trace grades | Upper bounds | traces-upper-bound | traces/traces_upper.tpe | The same pipeline under the allowance order, where a delay pays for operations at their upper runtime bound.
Trace grades | Intervals | traces-interval | traces/traces_intervals.tpe | The pipeline graded by a pair of a coverage and an allowance bound, compared componentwise.
Trace grades | Regular languages | traces-regex-symbolic | traces/regular_traces.tpe | A file-session and an authentication protocol, each graded by a regular language of operations and ticks.
Trace grades | Regular languages with costs | traces-regex-upper | traces/regex_costs.tpe | A sensor station graded by regular upper bounds whose ticks pay for operations at their upper runtime bounds.

Security levels | Levels | security-levels | levels/security_levels.tpe | A box at a security level is out of reach once a higher level has been touched since boxing.
Security levels | Embargoes | time-lower-bound-levels | levels/time_lower_levels.tpe | A box paired with a time lower bound and a level: an embargo with a taint check.
Security levels | Expiring capabilities | time-upper-bound-levels | levels/time_upper_levels.tpe | A box paired with a time upper bound and a level: a capability that expires and can be revoked by a taint.

Case study: 3D printing | Time bounds | time-lower-bound | 3dprint/3dprint.tpe | The stages of a 3D print, boxed at the lower time bounds each stage demands.
Case study: 3D printing | With effect handlers | time-lower-bound | 3dprint/3dprint_handlers.tpe | The same pipeline with each stage an operation, handled by clauses that respect its timing.
Case study: 3D printing | With trace grades | traces-interval | 3dprint/3dprint_traces.tpe | The same pipeline graded by the traces of operations it may exhibit, bounds on runtime included.
